From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Matkovich <sebastian.matkovich@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:57:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/omap: dispc: FIFO thresholds for manually updated panels
 on OMAP3

OMAP3's default overlay FIFO thresholds do not work for manually
updated panels: on the Nokia N950, whose DSI panel runs in command mode
(the LCD channel in stall mode), the panel is not refreshed at all.
dispc_ovl_compute_fifo_thresholds() already knows the thresholds for
manual updates on OMAP3 (FEAT_OMAP3_DSI_FIFO_BUG), but they are only
computed at init, for normal updates.

Set the manual update thresholds after an overlay is set up for an LCD
channel in stall mode, on SoCs with the OMAP3 DSI FIFO bug. The cause
in the hardware is not known; OMAP4 works with the defaults.

This is Sebastian Reichel's workaround ("drm/omap: plane: update fifo
size on ovl setup", v2, 2018) on today's dispc, using the existing
OMAP3 feature instead of a new flag. Untested on hardware.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/omapdrm/dss/dispc.c | 21 ++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/omapdrm/dss/dispc.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/omapdrm/dss/dispc.c
index cf0558150..4b3566fc2 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/omapdrm/dss/dispc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/omapdrm/dss/dispc.c
@@ -2770,8 +2770,27 @@ int dispc_ovl_setup(struct dispc_device *dispc,
 		oi->zorder, oi->pre_mult_alpha, oi->global_alpha,
 		oi->rotation_type, replication, vm, mem_to_mem,
 		oi->color_encoding, oi->color_range);
+	if (r)
+		return r;
 
-	return r;
+	/*
+	 * OMAP3's default FIFO thresholds do not work for manually updated
+	 * panels (an LCD channel in stall mode, such as a DSI panel in command
+	 * mode): the N950's panel is then not refreshed at all. With the
+	 * thresholds for manual updates it is. The cause in the hardware is
+	 * not known; OMAP4 works with the defaults.
+	 */
+	if (dispc_has_feature(dispc, FEAT_OMAP3_DSI_FIFO_BUG) &&
+	    dss_mgr_is_lcd(channel) &&
+	    mgr_fld_read(dispc, channel, DISPC_MGR_FLD_STALLMODE)) {
+		u32 low, high;
+
+		dispc_ovl_compute_fifo_thresholds(dispc, plane, &low, &high,
+						  false, true);
+		dispc_ovl_set_fifo_threshold(dispc, plane, low, high);
+	}
+
+	return 0;
 }
 
 int dispc_ovl_enable(struct dispc_device *dispc,
